  "acceptanceCriteria": [
    "A transition spec at .company/tasks/active/TASK-002/play-transition.md gives a beat-by-beat timeline for Play (time offsets in ms, property animated, easing, and owner element or object for each beat) covering page chrome exit, canvas growth to full screen, camera move from hero framing to the follow position, avatar turn and walk into the world, and HUD entry, totaling about 1.5 to 2.5 s once assets are ready.",
    "The spec defines the loading case (assets not ready when Play is clicked): what the user sees while waiting without a blocking screen, how progress and Cancel are shown, and how the sequence resumes when ready, plus prefetch of the game chunk on Play hover or focus.",
    "The spec defines Exit as the reverse sequence returning to the exact pre-Play hero layout, scroll position and focus, plus the prefers-reduced-motion variant and the mobile variant (touch controls entry).",
    "The spec maps each beat to the existing design (design.md sections for the shell, followCamera.beginEntry, the entering session state and scripted auto-walk) and lists the minimal additions, keeps game code out of the initial portfolio bundle, and names any risk to the talking-avatar hero.",
    "The spec lists measurable verification steps for QA (recorded frame sequence, no layout jump or hard cut, frame-time budget during the transition), and new content has no em dash or machine-local path."
  ],
